# Shell probe scripts
*.sh

# Compiled Cufet programs — `cufet build <file>.cufe` writes an extensionless binary next to its
# source, so it lands in the tree beside the file it was built from. One per buildable file here,
# named explicitly rather than by pattern: git has no way to say "extensionless", and a broad rule
# would swallow a future directory of the same name.
/tools/shell
/tools/repl
/tools/terminal

# What `cufet build` remembers, so it can skip a step nothing has changed: one line per step,
# holding its argv and the checksum of every path it needs. Machine-local and rebuildable —
# deleting it is the supported way to ask for a full rebuild, which is why there is no flag.
.cufet-build
